  "notes": "Qualified Dividends and Capital Gain Tax Worksheet line 13. The 15% ceiling for the filing status, reusing tax.us.2025.parameter.preferential-fifteen-ceiling v1 ($533,400 single, $300,000 married filing separately, $600,050 married filing jointly or qualifying surviving spouse, $566,700 head of household; 2025 Form 1040 instructions, worksheet line 13). v2 reads tax.us.2025.hoh.tests-met only when the filing status is head of household, and tax.us.2025.qss.tests-met only when it is qualifying surviving spouse. Yes publishes the same lookup as v1. No refuses the line (DEPENDENCY_INVALID, naming the answer so the page shows that question beside the refusal) rather than showing that status's ceiling. An unanswered answer blocks naming it. The worksheet states a ceiling for each filing status and does not give another status's ceiling when the checked status does not apply. Single, married filing jointly and married filing separately read nothing new."
